  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "2 Chronicles",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 20,
    "summary": "The Ammonites and others attack Judah—Jehoshaphat and all the people fast and pray—Jahaziel prophesies the deliverance of Judah—Judah’s attackers war among and destroy themselves.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "It came to pass after this also, that the children of Moab, and the children of Ammon, and with them other beside the Ammonites, came against Jehoshaphat to battle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37
          },
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:1",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Then there came some that told Jehoshaphat, saying, There cometh a great multitude against thee from beyond the sea on this side Syria; and, behold, they be in Hazazon-tamar, which is En-gedi.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 156
          },
          {
            "start": 181,
            "end": 183
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:2",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoshaphat feared, and set himself to seek the Lord, and proclaimed a fast throughout all Judah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Fast, Fasting."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Fast, Fasting.",
            "prettyString": "TG Fast, Fasting",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Fast, Fasting",
                "entryId": "tg-fast-fasting",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:3",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And Judah gathered themselves together, to ask help of the Lord: even out of all the cities of Judah they came to seek the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:4",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoshaphat stood in the congregation of Judah and Jerusalem, in the house of the Lord, before the new court,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:5",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And said, O Lord God of our fathers, art not thou God in heaven? and rulest not thou over all the kingdoms of the heathen? and in thine hand is there not power and might, so that none is able to withstand thee?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 79
          },
          {
            "start": 141,
            "end": 153
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:6",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Art not thou our God, who didst drive out the inhabitants of this land before thy people Israel, and gavest it to the seed of Abraham thy friend for ever?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 133,
            "text": "TG Seed of Abraham."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Seed of Abraham.",
            "prettyString": "TG Seed of Abraham",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Seed of Abraham",
                "entryId": "tg-seed-of-abraham",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:7",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And they dwelt therein, and have built thee a sanctuary therein for thy name, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:8",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "If, when evil cometh upon us, as the sword, judgment, or pestilence, or famine, we stand before this house, and in thy presence, (for thy name is in this house,) and cry unto thee in our affliction, then thou wilt hear and help.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 197,
            "text": "TG Affliction."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 143,
            "end": 145
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Affliction.",
            "prettyString": "TG Affliction",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Affliction",
                "entryId": "tg-affliction",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:9",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, behold, the children of Ammon and Moab and mount Seir, whom thou wouldest not let Israel invade, when they came out of the land of Egypt, but they turned from them, and destroyed them not;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:10",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I say, how they reward us, to come to cast us out of thy possession, which thou hast given us to inherit.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:11",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "O our God, wilt thou not judge them? for we have no might against this great company that cometh against us; neither know we what to do: but our eyes are upon thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 121,
            "text": "Heb. 11:8; 1 Ne. 4:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 150,
            "end": 153
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Heb. 11:8; 1 Ne. 4:6.",
            "prettyString": "Hebrews 11:8; 1 Nephi 4:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "hebrews",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 11,
                    "end": 11,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 8,
                        "end": 8
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1nephi",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:12",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And all Judah stood before the Lord, with their little ones, their wives, and their children.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:13",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Then upon Jahaziel the son of Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, a Levite of the sons of Asaph, came the Spirit of the Lord in the midst of the congregation;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:14",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said, Hearken ye, all Judah, and ye inhabitants of Jerusalem, and thou king Jehoshaphat, Thus saith the Lord unto you, Be not afraid nor dismayed by reason of this great multitude; for the battle is not yours, but God’s.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 196,
            "end": 202,
            "text": "1 Sam. 17:47; D&C 105:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 203,
            "end": 205
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Sam. 17:47; D&C 105:14.",
            "prettyString": "1 Samuel 17:47; D&C 105:14",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
