                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:15",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "To morrow go ye down against them: behold, they come up by the cliff of Ziz; and ye shall find them at the end of the brook, before the wilderness of Jeruel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "HEB ascent."
          },
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "OR wadi, valley."
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "OR east of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:16",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye shall not need to fight in this battle: set yourselves, stand ye still, and see the salvation of the Lord with you, O Judah and Jerusalem: fear not, nor be dismayed; to morrow go out against them: for the Lord will be with you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "OR deliverance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 42
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 74
          },
          {
            "start": 213,
            "end": 220
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:17",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoshaphat bowed his head with his face to the ground: and all Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem fell before the Lord, worshipping the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:18",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Levites, of the children of the Kohathites, and of the children of the Korhites, stood up to praise the Lord God of Israel with a loud voice on high.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 20:19",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And they rose early in the morning, and went forth into the wilderness of Tekoa: and as they went forth, Jehoshaphat stood and said, Hear me, O Judah, and ye inhabitants of Jerusalem; Believe in the Lord your God, so shall ye be established; believe his prophets, so shall ye prosper.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 184,
            "end": 191,
            "text": "TG Faith."
          },
          {
            "start": 242,
            "end": 249,
